.TH VXRWM 1 vxrwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
vxrwm \- Versatile Wayland window manager (dwm fork)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vxrwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-srcdir ]
.RB [ \-ignoreautostart ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
vxrwm is a versatile dynamic window manager for Wayland, forked from dwm and
ported onto the
.B river
window management protocol
.RB ( river\-window\-management\-v1 ,
.RB river\-xkb\-bindings\-v1
and
.BR river\-layer\-shell\-v1 ).
Run it as river's configuration command:
.PP
.RS
.EX
river \-c vxrwm
.EE
.RE
.PP
It adds quality-of-life features such as 8-sided resize, cursor warping,
enhanced floating toggle, gaps, fullscreen support and more \- all of which can
be enabled or disabled at compile time via simple defines in modules.h
(similar in spirit to dwm-flexipatch).

It manages windows in three layouts: tiled, monocle and floating. Layouts can
be switched dynamically to optimize for the current task or application.

In tiled layout, windows are arranged in a master area (left, one window by
default) and a stacking area (right). The number of master windows and master
area size are adjustable. Monocle maximizes all windows to screen size.
Floating allows free moving and resizing. Dialogs and certain window types are
always managed as floating.

Windows are organized by tags. Each window can have one or multiple tags;
viewing a tag (or set of tags) shows all windows with matching tags.

The status bar (per screen) displays tags, current layout symbol, focused
window titles, and status text read from a named pipe. Selected tags use
different colors; occupied tags and focused window tags are indicated with
squares.

A small border around windows shows focus state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.TP
.B \-srcdir
prints the source directory used to locate auxiliary files, then exits.
.TP
.B \-ignoreautostart
starts without running the modules.h autostart hook.
.SH STATUS
.TP
.B vxrwm reads status text from a named pipe and displays it in the right
hand side of the status bar. The path is taken from the
.B VXRWM_STATUS
environment variable and defaults to
.BI $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vxwm_status
(falling back to
.BR /tmp/vxwm_status ).
The pipe is created if it does not exist. Write to it with e.g.
.PP
.RS
.EX
echo "$(date)" > $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vxwm_status
.EE
.RE
.SH USAGE
.SS Status bar
.TP
.B VXRWM_STATUS
named pipe
is read and displayed in the status area (see
.BR STATUS ).
.TP
.B Button1
on tag → view only that tag  
on layout symbol → toggle tiled ↔ floating
.TP
.B Button3
on tag → add/remove that tag from view
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button1
on tag → apply tag to focused window
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
on tag → toggle tag on focused window
.SS Keyboard commands (default MODKEY = Mod4)
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-Return
Start
.BR st(1).
.TP
.B Mod4\-p
Spawn
.BR dmenu(1)
for launching programs.
.TP
.B Mod4\-b
Toggle bar visibility.
.TP
.B Mod4\-j / k
Focus next / previous window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-i / d
Increase / decrease number of master windows.
.TP
.B Mod4\-h / l
Decrease / increase master area factor.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Return
Zoom focused window to/from master area (tiled layouts only).
.TP
.B Mod4\-0
View previously selected tags.
.TP
.B Mod4\-t / f / m
Set layout tiled / floating / monocle.
.TP
.B Mod4\-space
Cycle to next layout.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-space
Toggle focused window floating ↔ tiled.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-c
Close focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-[1-9]
View windows on tag 1–9.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Tab
View all windows (all tags).
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-[1-9]
Toggle tag 1–9 into/out of view.
.TP
.B Mod1\-[1-9]
Apply tag 1–9 to focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-0
Apply all tags to focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-, / .
Focus previous / next monitor.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-, / .
Send focused window to previous / next monitor.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-q
Quit vxrwm.
.SS Mouse commands
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button1
Drag to move focused window (toggles tiled → floating).
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button2
Toggle floating state of focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
Drag to resize focused window (toggles tiled → floating).

When BETTER_RESIZE is enabled, resizing works from all 8 sides/corners.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
vxrwm is configured by editing
.B config.h
(keys, colors, rules, bar, etc.) and
.B modules.h
(enabling/disabling patches and features), then recompiling.  
This approach keeps vxrwm fast, minimal and secure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dwm (1),
.BR river (1),
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR st (1)
